<%# locals: (event:, registration: nil) %>
<%#
  The compact row: the status as its icon alone, the name, and one meta line. No count tags, which
  the legend's matrix reserves for a card: a row competes with every other row beneath it.

  The question is the exception, and it stands wherever `Registration#response_due?` puts it - a row is where they are looking when they decide. The past list puts it too, in the past tense: an event that has ended and that nobody concluded is still worth a roster, so there the question goes to anyone who has not said yes or no, and `EventsHelper#answer_prompt` carries the tense. `open_to_answers?` rules out the events somebody ended rather than the ones the clock did; it is checked here as well as in `events/_response` so a closed event's row draws no empty wrapper.

  Where the row puts no question, the member's registration stays an icon at the row's end, whatever its status, in the Who's coming? tally's colours: an answer in its status colour, a question in info, a reserved place in the page's ink.
  `list-col-wrap` puts the question on its own line under the row rather than in a column beside it.
  `col-start-2` pins it under the name: the grid places it in the column of the cell before it, so behind the pencil it would land in the pencil's column and widen it until the name had no room.
%>
<li id="<%= dom_id event %>" class="list-row">
  <%= status_icon event, label: event.status, class: "size-icon-standalone self-center text-icon-muted" %>

  <%# WHY: the name's link is stretched over the whole row, daisyUI's `list-row` being its positioned container, so pressing anywhere on it opens the event while a screen reader still meets one link; the map link, the pencil and the answer buttons in `events/_response` are each lifted above that overlay with `relative z-1`, so the gaps between them still open the event. %>
  <%# WHY: the name and the place each trim to one line, so every row stays two lines tall; the row opens the event's screen, which draws both whole. `min-w-0` lets the row's cell shrink so the trims can happen. %>
  <div class="min-w-0">
    <%= trimmed event.name, :a, href: group_event_path(event.group, event), class: "link link-hover block after:absolute after:inset-0" %>

    <div class="text-xs flex gap-1">
      <span class="flex-none"><%= event_schedule_start(event) %></span>
      <% if event.address %>
        <span class="flex-none">·</span>
        <%= trimmed event.address.name, :a, href: address_map_url(event.address), class: "link link-hover relative z-1 min-w-0", target: "_blank" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% response_due = registration&.response_due? && event.open_to_answers? %>
  <% if registration && !response_due %>
    <%= status_icon registration, label: registration.answered? ? "you said #{registration.status}" : registration_status_label(registration), class: "size-icon-control self-center #{status_ink(registration.status)}" %>
  <% end %>

  <%# Frame 4h's pencil, last in the row, for a reader `edit?` allows. WHY: 20px, the answer's size and a step under the event's 24px status, so it reads beside the answer without competing with the name. WHY: the margin takes the row's 16px gap, daisyUI's rather than a token, down to `controls` plus the pencil's own inset, which sets its glyph 20px from the answer's bare one, the glyph gap the event screen's roster keeps. %>
  <% if allowed_to?(:edit?, event) %>
    <%= link_to edit_group_event_path(event.group, event), class: "btn btn-ghost btn-circle btn-sm relative z-1 text-primary self-center ml-[calc(var(--spacing-controls)+var(--spacing-control-inset)-1rem)]", aria: { label: "Edit #{event.name}" } do %>
      <%= icon :edit, class: "size-icon-control" %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <% if response_due %>
    <div class="list-col-wrap col-start-2">
      <%= render "events/response", event: event, registration: registration %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</li>
